3D%22middle%22%3E45-64%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22520.0%22%20y%3D%22292.5%22%20width%3D%2236.0%22%20height%3D%2277.5%22%20fill%3D%22%231d4ed8%22%2F%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22558.0%22%20y%3D%22280.1%22%20width%3D%2236.0%22%20height%3D%2289.9%22%20fill%3D%22%23f59e0b%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22558.0%22%20y%3D%22390%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E65%2B%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22625%22%20y%3D%2270%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%231d4ed8%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22645%22%20y%3D%2282%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EMen%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22625%22%20y%3D%2290%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%23f59e0b%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22645%22%20y%3D%22102%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EWomen%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Weekly hours of exercise by age group
The average number of hours of exercise per week taken by men and women in five age groups in Westbury.
Unit: hours per week
Series | 16-24 | 25-34 | 35-44 | 45-64 | 65+
Men | 5.5 | 4 | 3.2 | 2.8 | 2.5
Women | 4.5 | 3.5 | 3 | 3.1 | 2.9
Main features: Men aged 16-24 exercised most (5.5 hours) and exercise fell with age for men, to 2.5 hours for over-65s. Women’s exercise also fell, to 3.0 hours at 35-44, but then levelled off (3.1 and 2.9 hours), so from age 45 women exercised more than men (3.1 v 2.8; 2.9 v 2.5). The gender gap was widest among the youngest group.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('ielts-b2-wt1-002', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'writing', 'ielts-writing-task1-figure', 'Describe the figure', 'Books borrowed from three libraries', 'The bar chart below shows the number of books borrowed from three branch libraries in Hollins in 2014 and 2024.

