How used paper is recycled into new paper products.
Stage 1: Used paper collected from homes and offices
Stage 2: Sorted by type and grade
Stage 3: Mixed with water to make pulp
Stage 4: Pulp screened to remove plastic and staples
Stage 5: Ink removed with air bubbles
Stage 6: Pulp spread on rollers and dried
Stage 7: Rolled into large reels
Stage 8: Cut and sent to factories
Main features: The process has eight stages, from collection to delivery to factories. Paper is collected and sorted, turned into pulp with water, cleaned of contaminants and ink, then pressed and dried on rollers before being rolled and cut into new products.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
