The stages in the production of honey.
Stage 1: Bees collect nectar from flowers
Stage 2: Nectar stored in the hive’s wax cells
Stage 3: Bees fan their wings to evaporate water
Stage 4: Cells sealed with wax
Stage 5: Beekeeper removes the frames
Stage 6: Wax caps cut off
Stage 7: Honey extracted by spinning
Stage 8: Honey filtered and put into jars
Main features: The process begins naturally in the hive, where bees collect nectar, store it, reduce its water content and seal it. The beekeeper then takes the frames, uncaps the cells, spins out the honey, and filters and bottles it. Four stages are natural and four are carried out by people.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
