The main stages in building a road tunnel under a river.
Stage 1: Survey of the riverbed and rock
Stage 2: Access shafts dug on both banks
Stage 3: Tunnel boring machine lowered into shaft
Stage 4: Machine cuts through rock
Stage 5: Concrete rings fitted to line the tunnel
Stage 6: Waste rock removed by conveyor
Stage 7: Road surface and lighting installed
Stage 8: Safety tests before opening
Main features: Construction begins with a survey and the digging of shafts on each bank. A boring machine then cuts the tunnel, with concrete rings fitted and waste rock removed as it advances. Finally the road, lighting and safety checks are completed before the tunnel opens.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
