22%20y1%3D%22255.0%22%20x2%3D%22372%22%20y2%3D%22255.0%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%20stroke-width%3D%222%22%20marker-end%3D%22url%28%23a%29%22%2F%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22218%22%20y%3D%22210%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%2290%22%20rx%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23eff6ff%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22234%22%20cy%3D%22226%22%20r%3D%2211%22%20fill%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22234%22%20y%3D%22230%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E7%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22246%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EPacked%20and%20delivered%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'How bricks are made
The process of manufacturing bricks.
Stage 1: Clay dug from the ground
Stage 2: Clay crushed and mixed with sand and water
Stage 3: Mixture pressed into moulds or cut by wire
Stage 4: Bricks dried for 24 to 48 hours
Stage 5: Fired in a kiln at 900-1,300°C
Stage 6: Cooled for 48 to 72 hours
Stage 7: Packed and delivered
Main features: Bricks are made in seven stages, beginning with digging clay and ending with delivery. The clay is mixed and shaped, then dried and fired in a kiln at up to 1,300°C before a long cooling period. Drying and cooling together take between three and five days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
