231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22234%22%20cy%3D%22226%22%20r%3D%2211%22%20fill%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22234%22%20y%3D%22230%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E7%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22246%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3ETea%20tasted%20and%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22261%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Egraded%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%22218%22%20y1%3D%22255.0%22%20x2%3D%22184%22%20y2%3D%22255.0%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%20stroke-width%3D%222%22%20marker-end%3D%22url%28%23a%29%22%2F%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%2230%22%20y%3D%22210%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%2290%22%20rx%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23eff6ff%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%2246%22%20cy%3D%22226%22%20r%3D%2211%22%20fill%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2246%22%20y%3D%22230%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E8%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22105.0%22%20y%3D%22246%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3ETea%20packed%20and%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22105.0%22%20y%3D%22261%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Eexported%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'How tea is produced
The production of black tea from leaf to packet.
Stage 1: Leaves picked by hand
Stage 2: Leaves spread out to wilt for 12-18 hours
Stage 3: Leaves rolled to break them
Stage 4: Leaves left to oxidise and turn brown
Stage 5: Leaves dried with hot air
Stage 6: Tea sorted by size
Stage 7: Tea tasted and graded
Stage 8: Tea packed and exported
Main features: Tea production has eight stages from picking to export. After picking, the leaves are wilted, rolled and oxidised, which changes their colour, and then dried with hot air. Finally the tea is sorted, graded by tasting and packed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
