('ielts-b2-lfb-032', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'listening', 'ielts-listening-fill-blanks', 'Fill in the blanks', 'Lecture: Desert plants', 'Listen and complete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer. This is a short practice drill with synthesised playback.', 180, 0, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['Original practice', 'IELTS', 'Listening'], 'The recording gives these answers in order: stems, night, widely. Do not include extra words.', NULL, NULL, 'Lecturer: Desert plants survive by storing water. Cacti store it in their stems, not their leaves, which have become spines. Many desert plants open their pores only at night, when it is cooler, to reduce water loss. Their roots are often shallow but spread very widely.', 'Cacti store water in their: ____ (1)
