('ielts-b2-lfb-033', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'listening', 'ielts-listening-fill-blanks', 'Fill in the blanks', 'Lecture: How penguins keep warm', 'Listen and complete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer. This is a short practice drill with synthesised playback.', 180, 0, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['Original practice', 'IELTS', 'Listening'], 'The recording gives these answers in order: air, fat, centre. Do not include extra words.', NULL, NULL, 'Lecturer: Emperor penguins survive Antarctic winters in which temperatures fall below minus forty degrees. Their dense feathers trap a layer of air, and a thick layer of fat lies beneath the skin. In the worst storms, thousands of birds huddle together, taking turns to move from the cold edge of the group to the warm centre.', 'Their feathers trap a layer of ____ (1)
