('ielts-b2-lfb-034', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'listening', 'ielts-listening-fill-blanks', 'Fill in the blanks', 'Lecture: The zip fastener', 'Listen and complete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer. This is a short practice drill with synthesised playback.', 180, 0, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['Original practice', 'IELTS', 'Listening'], 'The recording gives these answers in order: apart, teeth, boots. Do not include extra words.', NULL, NULL, 'Lecturer: Early designs for a sliding fastener were unreliable and often came apart. In 1913 the engineer Gideon Sundback produced a much better design, using interlocking teeth. The name zipper was first used for rubber boots that had the fastener, and only much later did zips become common on clothing.', 'Early fasteners often came ____ (1)
