('ielts-b2-lfb-035', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'listening', 'ielts-listening-fill-blanks', 'Fill in the blanks', 'Lecture: Earthworms and soil', 'Listen and complete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer. This is a short practice drill with synthesised playback.', 180, 0, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['Original practice', 'IELTS', 'Listening'], 'The recording gives these answers in order: water, nutrients, decades. Do not include extra words.', NULL, NULL, 'Lecturer: Earthworms are among the most important animals for healthy soil. As they burrow, they create tunnels that let air and water reach plant roots. They also eat dead leaves and produce casts that are rich in nutrients. Charles Darwin was so fascinated by them that he spent decades studying their behaviour.', 'Tunnels let air and ____ (1) reach plant roots
