('ielts-b2-lfb-036', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'listening', 'ielts-listening-fill-blanks', 'Fill in the blanks', 'Lecture: The kiwi', 'Listen and complete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer. This is a short practice drill with synthesised playback.', 180, 0, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['Original practice', 'IELTS', 'Listening'], 'The recording gives these answers in order: Zealand, beak, fifth. Do not include extra words.', NULL, NULL, 'Lecturer: The kiwi, a flightless bird found only in New Zealand, is unusual in many ways. Its nostrils are at the tip of its long beak, which it uses to smell insects and worms underground. The female lays an extremely large egg, which can weigh about a fifth of her body weight.', 'Found only in New ____ (1)
