('ielts-b2-lfb-039', 'ielts-2026-01', 'IELTS', ARRAY['IELTS'], 'listening', 'ielts-listening-fill-blanks', 'Fill in the blanks', 'Lecture: Morse code', 'Listen and complete the notes. Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer. This is a short practice drill with synthesised playback.', 180, 0, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['Original practice', 'IELTS', 'Listening'], 'The recording gives these answers in order: telegraph, dot, Baltimore. Do not include extra words.', NULL, NULL, 'Lecturer: Morse code was developed in the 1830s and 1840s for use with the electric telegraph. Letters are represented by combinations of short and long signals, known as dots and dashes. The most common letters were given the shortest codes; the letter E, for example, is a single dot. In 1844 the first long-distance message was sent from Washington to Baltimore.', 'It was developed for the electric ____ (1)
